  "last": {
    "advice": [
      "Use for a zstd-realized medium, dictionary-primed or explicitly dictionary-less.",
      "Avoid treating an absent gmeow:mediumDictionary as 'unknown' (it is the declared no-dictionary selection of that medium) and avoid varying the level per call — the level is declared on the medium precisely so it cannot drift per invocation.",
      "Mint the medium with one gmeow:mediumCodec from the zstd family, one gmeow:mediumZstdLevel, one gmeow:mediumSourceKind, and — for a per-rep medium — every gmeow:mediumDictionary its reps may select."
    ],
    "definition": "The zstd specialization of gmeow:Medium: a lawful (encode, decode) pair realized by a zstd-family codec at a declared compression level (gmeow:mediumZstdLevel) with an OPTIONAL dictionary set (gmeow:mediumDictionary). Optional means EXPLICITLY DECLARED, not absent: the dictionary-less medium is itself a named individual (gmeow:mediumProfileBaselineL12), so 'no dictionary' is a selection a frame makes, never a hole it falls into. The level is part of the declared medium because a level change is a byte-level change to every artifact the medium produces.",
    "id": "gmeow:ZstdDictMedium",
